ERRATUM for arm-C-7e01cf2e.json (#1619, 2026-09-16)

`queryCostMs.p50` and `queryCostMs.p95` in that file are BOTH THE MAXIMUM, not
percentiles. The capture predates commit a34eec38, which fixed the call into
`percentile` (it takes a FRACTION; the arm axis passed 50 and 95, so
`Math.ceil(309 * 50) - 1` clamped to the last index of the sorted samples).

  as recorded   p50 = p95 = 198.76 ms   -- the slowest of the 309 queries
  true values   p50 = 45.99 ms, p95 = 62.27 ms

The true values are re-derived from the 309 per-query `ms` values inside the
file itself (nearest rank, `eval/latency-stats.ts`). The measured rows are left
exactly as captured, so the file still parses through `parseArmRunReport` and
every other figure it carries -- recallAtK, mrr, imageNegativeLeakAt1 -- is
correct and re-derives exactly under the shipped definitions.

`pinParticipatingQueries: 0` beside `rag_pin_identifiers: true` is
configuration on, zero in effect: no query in the DE image fixture is an exact
identifier, so #1107's pin never fired. Do not cite this capture as evidence
that the pin was exercised.

Full context: README.md in this directory, "Errata on these two files".
